<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Help — Expense Reports</title>
  <%- include('partials/theme-init') %>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('partials/topbar') %>
  <div class="container">

    <div class="card">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0;">How this works</h2>
      <p>
        This app tracks your work expenses from receipt to reimbursement: upload a receipt,
        fill in a few details, group receipts into a report, and submit it when you're ready.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0;">1. Upload a receipt</h2>
      <p>
        Go to <a href="/receipts">Receipt Inbox</a> and choose a photo or PDF of your receipt — you can
        select several at once. Each one lands in your personal inbox and gets scanned automatically
        in the background to guess the date and total, so you usually don't have to type those in
        yourself. iPhone photos (HEIC) work fine; they're converted automatically.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0;">2. Fill in the details</h2>
      <p>
        Open a receipt from your inbox and check that the date and total look right (fix them if the
        scan got something wrong). Add the <strong>GL code</strong> and a <strong>description</strong> —
        both of these are what actually show up on the exported spreadsheet, so it's worth getting them
        right. Project name and notes are just for your own reference.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0;">3. Build a report</h2>
      <p>
        From <a href="/reports">My Reports</a>, start a new report (or open an existing draft), then
        check off the receipts from your inbox you want to include and add them. A report stays a
        <strong>draft</strong> — freely editable — until you submit it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0;">4. Submit and get reimbursed</h2>
      <p>
        Once a report has everything it needs, hit <strong>Submit</strong>. That locks it from further
        editing (you can always reopen it if you need to fix something). From the report page you can
        export it as an Excel spreadsheet or a PDF to hand off for reimbursement. Once you've actually
        been paid back, mark the report <strong>Paid</strong> to keep your records straight.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Your account</h2>
      <p>
        On the <a href="/account">Account</a> page, fill in your Employee # and Department — these feed
        the header of the exported spreadsheet, so it's worth setting them once up front. New accounts
        need an admin to approve them before they can log in.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
  <%- include('partials/footer') %>
  <script src="/js/theme.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
